## 2. Project identity and purpose

**System name:** VIRTUOLAB

**Full name:** Virtual ICT Learning and Computer Simulation System.

**Project title:**

Design and Development of a Web-Based Virtual ICT Learning and Computer Simulation System to Enhance Practical Computer Skills in Schools with Limited ICT Infrastructure in Zambia.

### Problem being addressed

Many schools in Zambia have limited access to computer laboratories, computers and other ICT learning equipment. Consequently, pupils may learn computer studies theoretically without sufficient opportunities to practise using computers and understand how computer systems operate.

This creates a gap between theoretical ICT knowledge and practical computer skills.

VIRTUOLAB should help address this challenge by providing an interactive virtual environment where pupils can learn computing concepts, explore computer hardware, understand operating systems and practise essential computer operations through browser-based simulations.

### Main objective

To design and develop an interactive web-based virtual ICT learning and computer simulation system that provides pupils with opportunities to acquire and practise fundamental computer skills in schools with limited ICT infrastructure.

### Important system principle

VIRTUOLAB is an educational simulation platform. It must not pretend to be a real Windows operating system or claim to replace actual computer hardware.

It should recreate selected computer operations in a realistic, interactive browser-based environment.

